# =====================================================================
# Release V077 -- Fix dummy-diary utilisation >100% (worked = booked)
# =====================================================================
# Dummy diary days (appt-only, no rota) were reading Diary Fill ~145% and Chair Util ~116%.
# Cause: the dummy "worked hours" used the first->last SPAN, which swept in gap + block time;
# the aggregate then subtracted block minutes on top -> denominator fell below the booked time.
#
# Fix (matches the intended design -- dummy days are 100% booked by definition):
#   * Diary load: dummy Available_Clinical_Mins = SUM of appointment durations (booked time),
#     not the span. Start/End_Time still show the first->last window.
#   * Aggregate: do NOT subtract block minutes from Worked_Hours on dummy days (Is_Dummy=1);
#     the booked time already excludes blocks.
# Result (dev T100): dummy-day Diary Fill ~100%, Chair Util 80%; all-time Chair Util 84% -> ~76%.
#
# Both are DROP/CREATE SP redeploys -> rebuild data via Orchestrate_Build.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V077__dummy_diary_worked_equals_booked.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY  Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Fact_Practitioner_Diaries.StoredProcedure.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Gold.usp_Load_Aggregate_Site_Patient_Practitioner_Daily.StoredProcedure.sql

TEST
